# Design exploration variants — not part of the shipped site
mockups/

# Local dev / editor
.claude/

# Local-only tooling: DB seed script + schema, never deployed
scripts/

# Prototypes — mostly not part of the shipped site. The agent portal ships
# (it needs to, to run its /api routes), and so does elevated.css it shares.
# Only the old draft apply/calculator pages stay local-only.
#
# Named explicitly rather than "prototypes/* + negate portal/" — a glob-then-
# negate pattern here silently drops everything under prototypes/portal/:
# ignore-file matching won't reliably re-include a nested directory's
# contents once a parent-level glob has excluded it, even with a trailing
# "/**" negation. Confirmed in production: prototypes/elevated.css (a
# directly-negated single file) served fine; every file under
# prototypes/portal/ 404'd.
prototypes/apply.html
prototypes/calculator.html

# Not part of the site. Some of these were being served publicly: the tests
# (internal pay logic) and the Palmetto logo, which is deliberately kept off
# the public site.
